---
description: Rata development workflow and source ownership
alwaysApply: true
---

- Read `AGENTS.md`, `AGENT_WORKBOOK.md`, `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/SECURITY.md`, and `docs/TASKS.md` before editing.
- Record active work in `AGENT_WORKBOOK.md` before material changes and update it with completed changes, validation, and blockers at handoff. Preserve other entries and never record secrets or sensitive user content.
- Run `npm run verify` before handing off a code change. Use `npm run dev` for Electron UI smoke testing.
- Keep React UI in `src/`, Electron composition in `electron/main.cjs`, native MVP adapters in `electron/mvp-tools.cjs`, runtime validators in `packages/contracts/`, and provider-independent runtime code in `packages/agent-core/`.
- Add behavioral tests under `tests/` and update documentation when a public contract or user-visible capability changes.
- Do not edit generated output under `dist/`, `release/`, or dependencies under `node_modules/`.
- Keep each change aligned to one ticket in `docs/TASKS.md`; avoid combining future provider, voice, bridge, and connector milestones.
